WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.582 --> 00:00:17.333
The servants had decorated the schoolroom for Sara's birthday party.

2
00:00:18.874 --> 00:00:21.616
Miss Minchin and Sara led all the girls inside.

3
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:26.060
Three servants, including Becky, followed the procession.

4
00:00:27.168 --> 00:00:30.830
The servants all carried boxes of presents, which they placed on a table.

5
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.652
Becky had forgotten herself in the midst of the excitement of the party.

6
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:40.415
Now she was grinning at Lottie, who was wriggling happily as she waited for Sara to open her

7
00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:43.217
presents. Miss Minchin frowned.

8
00:00:43.237 --> 00:00:48.219
"You may leave now," she told Becky and the other servants.

9
00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:53.963
"Please, Miss Minchin," Sara said suddenly, "may Becky stay?

10
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:56.384
I know she'd like to see the presents."

11
00:00:57.768 --> 00:01:00.889
Miss Minchin put on her glasses and looked Sara up and down.

12
00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:09.473
"Becky?" just a child too, you know," Sara added boldly.

13
00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:12.914
For a moment Miss Minchin didn't speak.

14
00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:17.356
"My dear Sara," she managed to say at last.

15
00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:20.957
"Kitchen maids are not children."

16
00:01:20.977 --> 00:01:26.920
"Well, Becky is a child," Sara repeated.

17
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.262
"Please let her stay because it's my birthday."

18
00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:35.106
Becky had been backing away, nervously twisting the bottom of her apron.

19
00:01:36.888 --> 00:01:38.249
The headmistress sighed.

20
00:01:38.269 --> 00:01:40.271
"Very well.

21
00:01:41.011 --> 00:01:43.834
As a birthday favor, she may stay.

22
00:01:44.514 --> 00:01:48.017
Becky, you must thank Miss Sara for her great kindness."

23
00:01:49.318 --> 00:01:51.620
At Miss Minchin's reply, her face lit up.

24
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.142
"I'm very grateful, miss!"

25
00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:57.800
she said, grinning at Sara.

26
00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.241
Miss Minchin waved her hand.

27
00:02:00.022 --> 00:02:02.163
It was in the direction of the corner near the door.

28
00:02:02.183 --> 00:02:05.926
"Stand over there, Becky," she commanded.

29
00:02:05.946 --> 00:02:08.687
"Away from the other girls!"

30
00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.293
Soon Miss Minchin left the room, and all the girls rushed toward the boxes.

31
00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.675
Sara opened the biggest one first.

32
00:02:21.456 --> 00:02:23.357
Inside was the Last Doll.

33
00:02:23.377 --> 00:02:27.480
"Oh!" groaned the children in delight.

34
00:02:28.576 --> 00:02:30.798
The new doll was truly magnificent.

35
00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:33.220
Lottie gasped.

36
00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.223
"She's almost as big as I am!"

37
00:02:36.243 --> 00:02:38.825
"She's dressed for the theater!"

38
00:02:39.245 --> 00:02:40.106
Ermengarde said.

39
00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:44.549
"Her cloak is lined with fur, and she has an opera glass."

40
00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.012
"Here's her trunk," said Sara.

41
00:02:48.032 --> 00:02:50.875
"Let's open it and look at her things."

42
00:02:52.196 --> 00:02:54.438
Sara sat on the floor and turned the key.

43
00:02:55.558 --> 00:02:57.020
The girls crowded around her.

44
00:02:57.976 --> 00:03:00.177
Never had the schoolroom been so noisy.

45
00:03:01.538 --> 00:03:04.300
Sara held up each item as she removed it from the trunk.

46
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:10.524
There were dresses, ballgowns, jewelry, hats, lace collars, and fans.

47
00:03:11.844 --> 00:03:15.206
Even Lavinia and Jessie were impressed by the contents of the trunk.

48
00:03:16.867 --> 00:03:19.149
Sara put a black velvet hat on the doll.

49
00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:24.352
"Let's pretend she understands that we're admiring her," she said.

50
00:03:25.696 --> 00:03:30.098
"You're always pretending things," Lavinia said in a superior tone.

51
00:03:31.198 --> 00:03:32.039
Sara looked up.

52
00:03:32.059 --> 00:03:34.300
"Yes, I am," she said.

53
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.821
"It's fun."

54
00:03:35.841 --> 00:03:39.782
"Well, it's easy to pretend if you're rich," said Lavinia.

55
00:03:39.802 --> 00:03:43.224
"Could you do it if you were a beggar and lived in an attic?"

56
00:03:44.744 --> 00:03:49.346
"I think I could, but it wouldn't be easy," Sara answered.

57
00:03:50.207 --> 00:03:52.608
Just then Miss Amelia came into the room.

58
00:03:53.648 --> 00:03:55.909
"Sara, your papa's lawyer, Mr.

59
00:03:55.929 --> 00:03:57.750
Barrow, has come to see Miss Minchin.

60
00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:00.431
Your birthday feast is ready in her sitting room.

61
00:04:01.011 --> 00:04:02.132
Lead the other girls there.

62
00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:03.892
Miss Minchin needs to meet with Mr.

63
00:04:03.912 --> 00:04:04.693
Barrow in here."

64
00:04:06.013 --> 00:04:07.414
Sara did as she was told.

65
00:04:11.255 --> 00:04:13.897
back to your work, Becky," said Miss Amelia.

66
00:04:14.637 --> 00:04:15.817
Then she left the room.

67
00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:18.879
Becky stayed behind in the room for a minute.

68
00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.357
Miss Amelia had told her to go back to work, but Becky couldn't help taking another look at

69
00:04:24.377 --> 00:04:24.798
the doll.

70
00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:30.141
She picked up the doll's hat and then a coat.

71
00:04:30.221 --> 00:04:32.102
Suddenly she heard Miss Minchin coming!

72
00:04:33.843 --> 00:04:35.163
Becky darted under the table.

73
00:04:36.004 --> 00:04:38.365
She hoped the tablecloth was long enough to hide her.

74
00:04:39.626 --> 00:04:44.929
The headmistress came into the room, followed by a small gentleman who looked rather disturbed.

75
00:04:44.949 --> 00:04:47.530
"Please have a seat, Mr.

76
00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:50.272
Barrow," Miss Minchin said as she sat down.

77
00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:51.872
But Mr.

78
00:04:51.912 --> 00:04:55.873
Barrow was too fascinated by the large doll and her wardrobe to sit.

79
00:04:55.893 --> 00:04:59.454
"Such a fancy gift for a child!"

80
00:04:59.474 --> 00:05:04.016
"Captain Crewe is a wealthy man," said Miss Minchin.

81
00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:07.997
"His diamond mines alone—" "Diamonds!"

82
00:05:08.557 --> 00:05:09.857
Mr. Barrow interrupted.

83
00:05:09.877 --> 00:05:13.078
"There were no diamonds in those mines.

84
00:05:13.358 --> 00:05:14.018
Never were."

85
00:05:14.038 --> 00:05:17.559
"What?" Miss Minchin stood up.

86
00:05:17.579 --> 00:05:19.020
"What do you mean?"

87
00:05:20.424 --> 00:05:22.946
"It was a bad investment," Mr.

88
00:05:22.986 --> 00:05:23.827
Barrow went on.

89
00:05:23.847 --> 00:05:29.311
"The late Captain Crewe—" Miss Minchin gasped.

90
00:05:29.331 --> 00:05:31.213
"'The late Captain Crewe'?

91
00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:33.935
You mean he's dead?"

92
00:05:33.955 --> 00:05:39.359
"Yes, that's what I've come to tell you," explained the lawyer coldly.

93
00:05:39.379 --> 00:05:44.644
"He died from jungle fever and stress caused by his business troubles.

94
00:05:45.184 --> 00:05:49.648
An old friend invested all Captain Crewe's money in the mines and then ran away.

95
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.061
Captain Crewe lost everything he owned."

96
00:05:54.781 --> 00:05:56.922
Miss Minchin dropped back into her chair.

97
00:05:56.942 --> 00:06:02.244
"Does this mean Sara is a pauper instead of a princess?"

98
00:06:02.724 --> 00:06:03.304
she cried.

99
00:06:03.324 --> 00:06:05.745
"Who will take care of her?"

100
00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:09.966
"You're responsible for her now," said Mr.

101
00:06:10.006 --> 00:06:14.147
Barrow. "She doesn't have a relative left in the world."
